  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 322 AM CDT Tue Jun 23 2026\n\nA stalled frontal boundary remains stretched west-east across our\nforecast area earlier this morning. Overnight convection has\nmostly spread west and east outside of our CWA boundaries, but\nrain remains possible along it. And a few thunderstorms may re-\ndevelop with heating south of the boundary this afternoon. A\ncomplex or two of thunderstorms is expected to develop along the\nfront in the broader region Wednesday, spreading into our forecast\narea during the day. There is a Marginal Risk for severe\nthunderstorms Wednesday associated with this possibility.\n\nThrough Thursday, the threat for dangerous heat will remain more \n\"Limited\" in nature - southern areas seeing heat index up to \naround 105 degrees. The heat will tick upwards for Friday/Saturday \nand especially by Sunday/Monday when heat index values are\nexpected to reach above 110 degrees for portions of the area. Be\nsure relatives and neighbors have cool places to stay this week. \n/NF/",
